      "labels": [
        {
          "text": "And this map is actually an intertwining operator, meaning that it commutes with",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            92.49,
            486.01,
            102.45
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "the action of G: since g and V are both representations of G this is a sensible thing",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            104.36,
            485.94,
            114.45
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
            "CMR10",
            "EUFM10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "to say, and it is easy to check.",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            116.37,
            257.16,
            126.33
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Pions act on nucleons via precisely such an intertwining operator:",
          "bbox": [
            141.0,
            128.37,
            428.04,
            138.33
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "sl(2, C) ⊗C2 →C2.",
          "bbox": [
            263.4,
            142.41,
            348.6,
            156.57
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMMI10",
