          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10",
            "CMTI10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Feynman diagrams are calculational tools in physics, though to actually use them",
          "bbox": [
            141.0,
            426.21,
            486.02,
            436.17
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "as such, we need quantum ﬁeld theory. Then, instead of just standing for intertwin-",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            438.21,
            486.08,
            448.17
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "ing operators between representations of compact groups such as SU(2), they depict",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            450.09,
            486.02,
            460.05
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "intertwining operators between representations of the product of this group and the",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            462.09,
            485.98,
            472.05
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Poincar´e group, which describes the symmetries of spacetime. Unfortunately, the",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            474.09,
            485.98,
            484.05
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "details are beyond the scope of this paper. By ignoring the Poincar´e group, we are,",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            485.97,
            486.12,
            495.93
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "in the language of physics, restricting our attention to ‘internal degrees of freedom’,",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            497.97,
            486.0,
            507.93
          ],
          "intersectsDrawing": false,
          "fonts": [
            "CMR10"
          ],
          "sizes": [
            9.96
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and their ‘internal’ (i.e., gauge) symmetries.",
          "bbox": [
            126.0,
            509.97,
